1
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:09,540
I wrote the wrong character!

2
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:11,260
Got an eraser?

3
00:00:11,260 --> 00:00:13,080
You can't erase ballpoint pen, you know.

4
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:15,540
Guess I'll just rub it out with spit.

5
00:00:15,540 --> 00:00:16,760
Gross!

6
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:18,980
That only made it dirtier.

7
00:00:18,980 --> 00:00:21,100
Guess I have no choice but
to scribble it out in black.

8
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:22,640
You're a total idiot.

9
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:25,700
Erasing an important document with spit?

10
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:28,160
Do you have any intelligence at all?

11
00:00:29,240 --> 00:00:31,660
You're being unusually strict today, Buchon.

12
00:00:32,940 --> 00:00:34,180
Read this.

13
00:00:34,180 --> 00:00:36,260
Whose is this awful handwriting?

14
00:00:36,260 --> 00:00:37,680
It's yours.

15
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:40,000
Mine? That's odd.

16
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,040
Did I really write like this?

17
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:43,680
Try to decipher it.

18
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:45,780
September 1st.

19
00:00:45,780 --> 00:00:47,360
This character is...

20
00:00:48,180 --> 00:00:50,580
Do you know how to read this character?

21
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:53,820
Don't write characters you
can't even read yourself.

22
00:00:53,820 --> 00:00:56,100
People who are sloppy with their handwriting

23
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:57,320
are also sloppy with their time,

24
00:00:58,160 --> 00:01:00,940
sloppy with money,
and so sloppy in how they live.

25
00:01:00,940 --> 00:01:02,060
That's you.

26
00:01:02,060 --> 00:01:04,280
That's prejudice! As long as handwriting can be read,
it's fine, right?

27
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:06,380
You can't read your own handwriting,
can you?

28
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:09,960
Compare it with Nakagawa's
and it's plain to see.

29
00:01:09,960 --> 00:01:10,900
Take a look.

30
00:01:11,280 --> 00:01:12,940
The final stroke is neatly stopped.

31
00:01:12,940 --> 00:01:14,860
The difference in character
shows in the writing.

32
00:01:14,860 --> 00:01:17,380
Yours is sloppy,
like you never bothered to stop the strokes.

33
00:01:18,080 --> 00:01:21,020
The parallel lines in the next
character are really well balanced.

34
00:01:21,020 --> 00:01:24,680
Yours has no parallel lines at all,
and the flicks are backwards.

35
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:27,480
This character is also beautifully balanced.

36
00:01:28,160 --> 00:01:30,940
Yours has gotten so bad it's not writing anymore,
it's a code.

37
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:34,440
And what's this horse race
prediction in the margin?

38
00:01:34,900 --> 00:01:38,140
Listen, rewrite the report by tomorrow.

39
00:01:38,140 --> 00:01:39,340
Got it?

40
00:01:43,040 --> 00:01:47,140
When you watch TV,
turn the lights on and sit farther back.

41
00:01:55,840 --> 00:02:00,260
Anyone short on money, come to me.

42
00:02:00,260 --> 00:02:04,960
I don't have any either, so don't worry.

43
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:08,820
Look at the blue sky.

44
00:02:08,820 --> 00:02:12,060
White clouds.

45
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:44,360
You idiot!

46
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:47,620
You really are something else.

47
00:02:48,020 --> 00:02:50,840
I told you to submit it by today, didn't I?

48
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:55,020
You live such a sloppy life,
without a shred of responsibility,

49
00:02:55,020 --> 00:02:56,540
so this is what happens.

50
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:59,360
Senpai, what did you do this time?

51
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:03,000
You forgot the report Chief
Ohara told you to rewrite,

52
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:04,680
apparently because you
were playing pachinko.

53
00:03:05,220 --> 00:03:07,920
You're finishing it tonight, no matter what.

54
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:10,460
Got it, Ryotsu?
No matter how many hours it takes.

55
00:03:12,060 --> 00:03:13,180
Fine, I'll do it.

56
00:03:13,180 --> 00:03:16,200
Look, that character there is wrong.

57
00:03:17,060 --> 00:03:19,980
What's with this handwriting?
It looks like a worm doing the hula.

58
00:03:20,440 --> 00:03:22,360
Don't try to cover it up by drawing manga.

59
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:28,320
Finally finished.

60
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:31,260
I can't believe writing a
report wore you out this much.

61
00:03:31,640 --> 00:03:32,920
What a hopeless guy you are.

62
00:03:35,220 --> 00:03:37,180
Chief, what is this?

63
00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:39,820
Can't you tell? It's a written apology.

64
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:42,560
Because you were playing
pachinko during work hours.

65
00:03:44,220 --> 00:03:46,400
Senpai, I'm heading out now.

66
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:48,040
Good luck, Ryo-chan.

67
00:03:49,220 --> 00:03:50,220
You two.

68
00:03:50,660 --> 00:03:54,000
Stop your chatter and hurry up
and write that written apology!

69
00:03:55,140 --> 00:03:58,980
By the way, Chief, where did you
decide on for the police box trip?

70
00:03:59,940 --> 00:04:01,500
The police box trip, you say?

71
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:02,820
No way, Kei-chan.

72
00:04:02,820 --> 00:04:06,200
You said where we're going is a big surprise you'd enjoy,
didn't you?

73
00:04:06,760 --> 00:04:07,800
W-what?

74
00:04:08,580 --> 00:04:11,720
Right. Then I'll be looking forward to it.

75
00:04:11,920 --> 00:04:13,480
Well then, I'm heading out now.

76
00:04:17,860 --> 00:04:19,318
What's wrong, Chief?

77
00:04:19,368 --> 00:04:22,660
You're not going to tell me you forgot,
are you?

78
00:04:23,180 --> 00:04:26,900
You're the one who calls others irresponsible and sloppy,
so go on and say it.

79
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:28,240
Chief!

80
00:04:28,740 --> 00:04:31,840
I did forget. What do we do, Ryotsu?

81
00:04:32,100 --> 00:04:33,540
Then,

82
00:04:33,590 --> 00:04:36,200
let's pretend this apology
letter never existed.

83
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:37,040
What?

84
00:04:37,800 --> 00:04:39,034
Well, isn't that right?

85
00:04:39,084 --> 00:04:43,080
You forgot something important too,
Chief, so we're even.

86
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:45,800
That's a completely different matter.

87
00:04:45,900 --> 00:04:46,961
I see.

88
00:04:47,011 --> 00:04:50,900
Everyone was looking forward to this trip,
you know.

89
00:04:52,300 --> 00:04:54,540
That's why I'm asking what we should do.

90
00:04:54,760 --> 00:04:59,000
At this point,
we won't be able to book lodging anywhere.

91
00:04:59,320 --> 00:05:00,720
Isn't there some way out?

92
00:05:01,080 --> 00:05:05,440
I was impressed by a saying
you always use, Chief.

93
00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:09,800
You know, the one about cleaning
up your own messes yourself.

94
00:05:10,260 --> 00:05:19,560
Sure, I said that, but it depends on the situation.
Leave it to me, and I'll find a way to save your face, Chief.

95
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:21,820
So this is the "disposal office,"

96
00:05:29,220 --> 00:05:31,240
Don't worry, Chief.

97
00:05:31,240 --> 00:05:33,980
Leave everything to me and it'll be fine.

98
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:35,800
I see.

99
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:39,720
So how much did we have
saved up for the trip fund?

100
00:05:40,300 --> 00:05:45,420
I completely forgot to deduct the
savings from everyone's salaries.

101
00:05:45,420 --> 00:05:46,820
So that means...

102
00:05:46,820 --> 00:05:48,540
The budget is zero!

103
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:52,480
I just remembered I have an errand.

104
00:05:53,180 --> 00:05:57,080
Please, Ryotsu, you're my only hope.
Only you.

105
00:05:57,920 --> 00:06:00,600
Fine, I'll do something about it.

106
00:06:02,280 --> 00:06:05,620
I'm counting on you.
It's a promise between men.

107
00:06:07,540 --> 00:06:10,220
Ryo-san's Kitamachi trip.

108
00:06:14,300 --> 00:06:18,400
Now then, we set off on the Kameari
Kōen-mae Police Box's annual trip.

109
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:22,840
Today's trip is special,

110
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:25,860
planned to help us take a fresh look

111
00:06:27,660 --> 00:06:30,380
at Tokyo, this megacity we live in.

112
00:06:30,380 --> 00:06:31,700
Tokyo?

113
00:06:32,660 --> 00:06:35,600
So we don't leave the area
inside the Yamanote Line?

114
00:06:35,920 --> 00:06:38,400
Exactly. It's so short, we think we know it,

115
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:40,520
but Tokyo is surprisingly unknown, isn't it?

116
00:06:40,520 --> 00:06:42,080
If we're police protecting the capital,

117
00:06:42,080 --> 00:06:44,540
we need to know Tokyo better.

118
00:06:44,540 --> 00:06:45,760
Otherwise, we can't keep it safe.

119
00:06:50,080 --> 00:06:51,360
Good idea.

120
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:53,340
Thank you for your support.

121
00:06:54,440 --> 00:06:57,340
And when it comes to Tokyo, leave it to me.

122
00:06:57,660 --> 00:07:00,520
I swiped Coke from the
occupation troops in Tokyo.

123
00:07:00,520 --> 00:07:05,440
Me, the boy said to be the
first in Japan to drink Coke!

124
00:07:05,440 --> 00:07:07,040
Is that really true, Ryo-san?

125
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:09,140
You weren't even born yet, Ryo-chan.

126
00:07:10,960 --> 00:07:12,860
That's enough of the preamble.

127
00:07:12,860 --> 00:07:17,060
The detailed itinerary is in the
handmade pamphlet I handed out earlier.

128
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:22,980
It says we'll first tour
Tokyo's traditional sites.

129
00:07:22,980 --> 00:07:25,200
I wonder if we'll see kabuki or noh.

130
00:07:25,860 --> 00:07:27,720
Next is a river cruise!

131
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:32,200
After that, it says we'll stroll
through Japan's biggest outlet mall.

132
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:34,600
And to finish, an all-you-can-drool buffet!

133
00:07:35,300 --> 00:07:36,500
Are you sure about this?

134
00:07:37,700 --> 00:07:39,300
Well then, off we go, full of energy!

135
00:07:39,300 --> 00:07:40,400
Yes, sir!

136
00:07:41,220 --> 00:07:42,220
Hold on a second.

137
00:07:42,220 --> 00:07:43,740
Where do you think you're going?

138
00:07:43,740 --> 00:07:45,040
Buy the tickets.

139
00:07:45,040 --> 00:07:46,740
We're taking the train, right?

140
00:07:46,740 --> 00:07:47,640
Naive.

141
00:07:47,640 --> 00:07:50,780
You two don't understand
the purpose of this trip.

142
00:07:50,780 --> 00:07:52,240
We're not buying tickets.

143
00:07:52,240 --> 00:07:53,980
We're walking straight past the station.

144
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:57,180
Apparently so

145
00:07:57,180 --> 00:07:58,620
On foot, no less?

146
00:08:00,080 --> 00:08:03,540
Come on, walking's good for your health too.

147
00:08:03,540 --> 00:08:07,240
A trip like this is exactly
what befits a police officer.

148
00:08:07,240 --> 00:08:09,520
Now, no complaining, let's walk.

149
00:08:09,520 --> 00:08:24,660
Wow, was this episode filmed in Ueno?

150
00:08:26,200 --> 00:08:28,820
The sea used to be right
next to this area too.

151
00:08:29,360 --> 00:08:29,760
Really?

152
00:08:30,980 --> 00:08:32,260
Just like the senior officer.

153
00:08:32,820 --> 00:08:33,220
Really?

154
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:34,700
Hey, hey.

155
00:08:34,700 --> 00:08:37,800
Maybe he's Ryo-chan's ancestor, you know.

156
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:43,780
Sure, we did see some history,
but what's this tradition?

157
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:47,960
Tradition means customs that have
been passed down since long ago.

158
00:08:47,960 --> 00:08:48,740
In other words,

159
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,780
this is Japan's tradition!

160
00:08:51,780 --> 00:08:53,300
Throwing beans to the pigeons!

161
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:57,040
I've never heard of that tradition.

162
00:08:57,040 --> 00:08:58,480
And the pigeons, too.

163
00:08:58,480 --> 00:09:00,180
They're running away, senpai!

164
00:09:00,180 --> 00:09:02,800
I see, this really is tradition.

165
00:09:02,800 --> 00:09:06,860
Every Japanese person has to throw
beans to the pigeons at least once.

166
00:09:06,860 --> 00:09:11,620
Typical Chief, holding out your hand. I'll
be collecting the beans' fee later, you know.

167
00:09:13,820 --> 00:09:16,900
That water cruise listed in the pamphlet...

168
00:09:17,420 --> 00:09:18,980
I guess it's this one.

169
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:24,040
All we do is walk and row,
it's so exhausting.

170
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:25,600
Should I go get it?

171
00:09:30,120 --> 00:09:33,880
Senpai,
stop staring at the sky and row too, please!

172
00:09:36,720 --> 00:09:41,920
Looking at the sky like this reminds me of
the Ryotsuke Rebellion from my childhood.

173
00:09:41,920 --> 00:09:43,280
The Ryotsuke Rebellion.

174
00:09:43,280 --> 00:09:45,580
Senpai, what's that?

175
00:09:46,440 --> 00:09:48,999
Back then,
inside a department store in Okachimachi,

176
00:09:49,049 --> 00:09:52,800
there was talk of opening a branch
of our family's tsukudani shop.

177
00:09:55,340 --> 00:09:58,340
We borrowed from the bank and pawned
the one thing that was truly valuable,

178
00:09:58,460 --> 00:10:00,386
the one Dad always bragged about,

179
00:10:00,436 --> 00:10:03,022
the imported pocket watch.

180
00:10:03,072 --> 00:10:04,720
We scraped together every yen we could.

181
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:06,808
But,

182
00:10:06,858 --> 00:10:10,634
he blew every last yen of that
money on horse racing and sake,

183
00:10:10,684 --> 00:10:12,940
and it was all gone in a single night.

184
00:10:13,400 --> 00:10:19,080
Dad got chased around by Mom, and in the end he jumped
from Higashi Bridge into the Sumida River to escape.

185
00:10:19,720 --> 00:10:22,000
It was truly a crisis for the family.

186
00:10:22,840 --> 00:10:27,720
In the end, the branch office plan and the
pocket watch he treasured were both ruined.

187
00:10:28,280 --> 00:10:32,900
I suppose Dad got carried away when he
saw so much money he wasn't used to holding.

188
00:10:33,460 --> 00:10:35,280
He's just like Ryo-chan, somehow.

189
00:10:35,660 --> 00:10:37,560
So what did you do, senpai?

190
00:10:38,020 --> 00:10:41,020
I just stayed here in the boat,
napping the whole time.

191
00:10:42,940 --> 00:10:45,140
I could never do something like that.

192
00:10:46,580 --> 00:10:48,440
If we'd opened that branch back then...

193
00:10:48,440 --> 00:10:50,980
I might be a branch manager by now.

194
00:10:50,980 --> 00:10:51,800
That's true.

195
00:10:55,760 --> 00:10:58,340
We've already lost half a day in Ueno alone.

196
00:10:58,340 --> 00:11:00,260
I'd like to take a little break.

197
00:11:00,260 --> 00:11:02,320
We're still moving on to the next place!

198
00:11:02,320 --> 00:11:05,140
Only you are fired up, senpai.

199
00:11:05,140 --> 00:11:07,020
Well, what's the harm?

200
00:11:07,960 --> 00:11:08,800
Next up is

201
00:11:09,340 --> 00:11:12,440
the best outlet mall in Japan,
though the budget was set up for it,

202
00:11:13,560 --> 00:11:14,740
just as I thought.

203
00:11:15,260 --> 00:11:17,400
Alright, from here on it's free time!

204
00:11:17,400 --> 00:11:19,560
Meet back at this spot in one hour.

205
00:11:19,560 --> 00:11:21,600
Free time, you say,

206
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:24,360
but we'll get pushed along
and swept away by this crowd!

207
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:27,880
Ryotsu, what are we supposed to do?

208
00:11:35,100 --> 00:11:35,880
There they are!

209
00:11:35,880 --> 00:11:37,280
Hey, Ryotsu!

210
00:11:37,280 --> 00:11:39,040
What is it?

211
00:11:39,040 --> 00:11:41,520
This is just too much, no matter what.

212
00:11:42,940 --> 00:11:45,620
On top of paying the entrance fees
and the boat fare out of my own pocket,

213
00:11:45,620 --> 00:11:47,200
it's nothing but nonsense!

214
00:11:47,760 --> 00:11:50,240
Well, what do you expect
when the budget's at zero?

215
00:11:50,240 --> 00:11:52,720
We have no choice but to have
everyone pay their own way.

216
00:11:53,380 --> 00:11:54,400
But, you see...

217
00:11:54,400 --> 00:11:58,320
Since you left it to me,
Chief, please don't interfere.

218
00:11:58,320 --> 00:11:59,220
Ryotsu...

219
00:12:07,320 --> 00:12:10,260
Idiot! Where are you looking?

220
00:12:10,260 --> 00:12:11,660
Hey, it was you, wasn't it?

221
00:12:13,120 --> 00:12:14,100
No, Dad!

222
00:12:14,180 --> 00:12:14,860
You idiot son!

223
00:12:15,500 --> 00:12:18,480
Aren't you needed at the shop?!
Loafing around here like this!

224
00:12:18,780 --> 00:12:21,100
You're the one who's come slacking off again,
aren't you!

225
00:12:21,480 --> 00:12:25,900
You reek of booze! Skimming money from the
shop again and drinking in broad daylight!

226
00:12:26,180 --> 00:12:29,440
Shut up! Lecturing your own father,
you've got some nerve!

227
00:12:29,860 --> 00:12:31,560
Dadadadadada!

228
00:12:32,380 --> 00:12:33,320
That's awful!

229
00:12:33,640 --> 00:12:35,160
So you went and did that, didn't you!

230
00:12:35,980 --> 00:12:38,680
Hey! No way I'm letting
you get away with that!

231
00:12:39,280 --> 00:12:40,640
Hey! So you've lost your way, have you!

232
00:12:40,640 --> 00:12:42,760
Aaaaah! Seriously, screw you!

233
00:12:43,700 --> 00:12:45,560
As if I'd get caught, you idiot!

234
00:12:45,560 --> 00:12:46,200
Aaaaah!

235
00:12:47,200 --> 00:12:47,940
Put it on the tab!

236
00:12:48,360 --> 00:12:49,060
I'm going home!

237
00:12:49,760 --> 00:12:50,800
What the hell do you think you're doing!

238
00:12:51,060 --> 00:12:52,000
Get down on your knees!

239
00:12:52,220 --> 00:12:53,800
Which one of us is the
one who's serious here!

240
00:12:55,700 --> 00:12:56,320
Going home!

241
00:12:56,640 --> 00:12:59,880
W-what on earth is all this commotion?

242
00:13:08,060 --> 00:13:10,340
You'd dare raise your hand to your own father,
you bastard!

243
00:13:10,400 --> 00:13:10,880
Is that okay?!

244
00:13:11,020 --> 00:13:12,560
Don't lay a hand on the kid!

245
00:13:12,620 --> 00:13:13,600
Is that okay, you bastard?!

246
00:13:20,720 --> 00:13:24,140
Everyone, I'm a police officer.
The commotion is over.

247
00:13:24,140 --> 00:13:25,480
Police? What police?

248
00:13:25,480 --> 00:13:28,540
That's right.
Resisting will only make it a crime.

249
00:13:33,020 --> 00:13:35,300
This one is the senpai's father.

250
00:13:40,340 --> 00:13:44,280
No matter where you go,
you cause trouble, you damn idiot.

251
00:13:44,280 --> 00:13:46,220
Don't mind it, don't mind it.

252
00:13:46,220 --> 00:13:48,320
After all, today is our company outing.

253
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:52,260
A model police officer who takes a
fresh look at Tokyo from the ground up.

254
00:13:52,260 --> 00:13:54,000
You understand, Chief?

255
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:56,320
This too, since the Chief forgot about it.

256
00:13:57,660 --> 00:14:00,020
Rediscover Tokyo from the ground up,
you say?

257
00:14:00,020 --> 00:14:02,640
With all due respect, if that's the case,

258
00:14:02,640 --> 00:14:04,100
then it's my time to shine, isn't it?

259
00:14:04,100 --> 00:14:06,220
What do you want, old man? Get lost!

260
00:14:06,220 --> 00:14:08,400
Ueno first, you fool!

261
00:14:08,840 --> 00:14:10,380
We'll tour the art museum

262
00:14:10,380 --> 00:14:12,100
and in front of the Saigo statue,

263
00:14:12,100 --> 00:14:13,160
feed beans to the pigeons.

264
00:14:14,400 --> 00:14:17,420
What? Then at Shinobazu Pond,
we'll take a boat

265
00:14:17,420 --> 00:14:18,140
ride.

266
00:14:18,140 --> 00:14:20,660
Damn it, then at Ameyoko

267
00:14:20,660 --> 00:14:23,180
So you went and pulled that off too

268
00:14:23,580 --> 00:14:25,580
There's no room for you here, Dad.

269
00:14:25,580 --> 00:14:26,880
Alright, off you go, shoo!

270
00:14:27,980 --> 00:14:30,860
Treating your own parent like a nuisance,
what a son you are!

271
00:14:30,860 --> 00:14:33,420
Don't you ever set foot in this house again!

272
00:14:33,920 --> 00:14:35,520
And don't come back!

273
00:14:35,980 --> 00:14:38,620
By the way, senpai, it's already evening.

274
00:14:38,620 --> 00:14:40,420
Where are we staying tonight?

275
00:14:41,520 --> 00:14:42,760
Asakusa!

276
00:14:44,420 --> 00:14:52,920
Staying at a hotel is, well, more or less the plan.
Come on, let's take the train instead of walking again.

277
00:14:52,920 --> 00:14:58,440
No way, this trip only means something if we walk!
Right, Bucchan?

278
00:14:58,440 --> 00:15:03,480
Right, it's only 23 kilometers, everyone.
Come on, let's walk!

279
00:15:07,680 --> 00:15:11,900
Doesn't Chief Ohara seem
awfully partial to senpai today?

280
00:15:11,900 --> 00:15:15,020
Yeah, I wonder if he has
some kind of hold on him.

281
00:15:15,020 --> 00:15:19,500
Senpai's talent for exploiting other people's weaknesses is second to none,
after all.

282
00:15:26,560 --> 00:15:28,180
Well, here's our lodging.

283
00:15:28,180 --> 00:15:30,100
Isn't this your senpai's family home?

284
00:15:30,620 --> 00:15:33,500
That's right, as long as there's a roof and futons,
that's enough, right?

285
00:15:34,060 --> 00:15:38,380
But the travel pamphlet says
dinner is an all-you-can-eat buffet.

286
00:15:38,380 --> 00:15:41,620
Of course, I never lie.

287
00:15:46,460 --> 00:15:50,340
At the tsukudani buffet,
you can eat any of these.

288
00:15:50,340 --> 00:15:51,860
Tsukudani buffet.

289
00:15:52,800 --> 00:15:53,900
Yo, we're here!

290
00:15:55,140 --> 00:15:58,100
Hey, you bastard,
don't you pull that shit again!

291
00:16:00,400 --> 00:16:02,360
Six people are staying tonight, so.

292
00:16:02,360 --> 00:16:04,680
If that's the case, you should've said so.

293
00:16:04,680 --> 00:16:06,340
But what are we going to do?

294
00:16:06,340 --> 00:16:08,240
Our place is cramped, you know.

295
00:16:08,240 --> 00:16:10,040
There's not even a place for me to sleep.

296
00:16:10,040 --> 00:16:11,420
It's fine, it's fine.

297
00:16:11,420 --> 00:16:13,060
Leave it to me.

298
00:16:17,760 --> 00:16:18,900
Well then, everyone,

299
00:16:18,900 --> 00:16:21,120
as I informed you earlier,

300
00:16:21,120 --> 00:16:24,260
each of you was to bring one food item,
correct?

301
00:16:24,260 --> 00:16:26,740
I brought mine, but...

302
00:16:26,740 --> 00:16:29,340
just dump it all into the pot.

303
00:16:30,260 --> 00:16:32,780
But mine's cookies.

304
00:16:33,720 --> 00:16:35,880
I brought steamed buns.

305
00:16:35,880 --> 00:16:38,560
I splurged on a melon.

306
00:16:38,960 --> 00:16:41,320
I brought bananas I
bought earlier at Ameyoko.

307
00:16:41,320 --> 00:16:43,500
I brought caviar, though.

308
00:16:44,660 --> 00:16:48,560
Never mind, I'll just throw
everyone's stuff into the pot!

309
00:16:50,900 --> 00:16:52,680
Well, it's just like a yami-nabe.

310
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:56,460
Whatever you pick up with your chopsticks,
you have to eat.

311
00:17:05,740 --> 00:17:07,000
Sorry, everyone.

312
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:09,180
I was the one who was wrong.

313
00:17:09,740 --> 00:17:10,560
Chief.

314
00:17:10,560 --> 00:17:13,120
Actually,

315
00:17:15,540 --> 00:17:17,720
So it was like that after all

316
00:17:17,720 --> 00:17:20,340
I had a feeling something was off.

317
00:17:20,340 --> 00:17:21,660
I'm so embarrassed.

318
00:17:21,660 --> 00:17:24,360
I'm an idiot for leaving
it to a guy like this.

319
00:17:24,360 --> 00:17:25,960
"A guy like this"? Come on, Chief.

320
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:29,320
Still, it was fun in its own way, wasn't it?

321
00:17:29,320 --> 00:17:30,820
Hey, to Hanta...

322
00:17:30,820 --> 00:17:32,820
and we got some nice souvenirs too.

323
00:17:33,700 --> 00:17:34,100
Yeah, that's right.

324
00:17:37,560 --> 00:17:38,440
Sorry.

325
00:17:38,440 --> 00:17:40,180
Well, a lot has happened,

326
00:17:40,180 --> 00:17:42,200
but let's wrap things up with a fun meal.

327
00:17:42,200 --> 00:17:45,500
Are we really still eating this?

328
00:17:45,780 --> 00:17:46,880
Of course.

329
00:17:46,880 --> 00:17:48,780
I'm the one in charge of this trip.

330
00:17:48,780 --> 00:17:51,560
We're eating this meal
as originally planned,

331
00:17:51,560 --> 00:17:55,740
the traditional closing meal of
the Kameari Kōen-mae Hashutsujo trip.

332
00:17:58,200 --> 00:17:58,260
Got it?

333
00:17:58,860 --> 00:17:59,960
Aaaaaaah!

334
00:18:06,320 --> 00:18:14,500
The melon's pretty good. You can really eat it, Ryo-san.
This guy ate anything since he was a kid.

335
00:18:15,080 --> 00:18:19,980
Hey, Chief, this guy won't listen to me.
So go ahead and knock him flat!

336
00:18:21,620 --> 00:18:24,220
You don't need to say unnecessary things.

337
00:18:25,420 --> 00:18:26,540
Oh.

338
00:18:26,540 --> 00:18:27,660
You bastard, what do you think you're doing!

339
00:18:30,860 --> 00:18:32,640
Wanna go? Come on, then!

340
00:18:33,260 --> 00:18:35,500
How dare you do this to your own father!

341
00:18:35,500 --> 00:18:37,260
I've had enough!

342
00:18:40,440 --> 00:18:41,660
Here we go again.

343
00:18:41,660 --> 00:18:43,780
Come on, everyone, this way, this way.

344
00:18:43,780 --> 00:18:47,940
Are you all really going to eat that strange,
unidentified stuff?

345
00:18:47,940 --> 00:18:50,100
Please, I'm begging you.

346
00:18:50,100 --> 00:18:52,000
Let's eat rice with tsukudani.

347
00:18:56,340 --> 00:18:58,200
It's a comforting smell, isn't it.

348
00:18:59,940 --> 00:19:05,140
I feel bad for Ryo-chan.
Well, never mind, don't worry about it.

349
00:19:06,540 --> 00:19:07,420
They're at it again.

350
00:19:08,300 --> 00:19:09,580
Oh oh!

351
00:19:18,460 --> 00:19:20,480
Looks like it's finally over.

352
00:19:22,560 --> 00:19:23,280
Mm...

353
00:19:26,280 --> 00:19:26,820
Aaaaaah.

354
00:19:28,840 --> 00:19:30,660
It hurts right where you kicked me.

355
00:19:33,640 --> 00:19:38,660
Good night, good night,
good night, good night.

356
00:19:39,260 --> 00:19:42,380
Goo-ood night... good night.

357
00:19:46,680 --> 00:19:52,180
If you move again, I'll put you out for good.
And you stop snoring and grinding your teeth.

358
00:19:55,180 --> 00:19:56,280
A shooting star!

359
00:19:56,280 --> 00:20:00,620
Look, over there too!

360
00:20:00,620 --> 00:20:01,360
Where?

361
00:20:02,520 --> 00:20:05,340
What, has your presbyopia
gotten so bad you can't see it?

362
00:20:05,340 --> 00:20:07,360
Don't be ridiculous, I can see it.

363
00:20:11,140 --> 00:20:12,480
Hey, Dad.

364
00:20:14,200 --> 00:20:16,860
We used to watch shooting stars here all the time,
didn't we.

365
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:19,100
Yeah, we did.

366
00:20:28,500 --> 00:20:29,880
Dad, there's a fire!

367
00:20:36,620 --> 00:20:38,880
Move aside, move aside!
Where's the source of the fire?

368
00:20:38,880 --> 00:20:40,640
The shop's kitchen is -

369
00:20:40,640 --> 00:20:43,240
Someone call 119!

370
00:20:43,240 --> 00:20:44,700
Pops, let's go.

371
00:20:44,700 --> 00:20:45,320
Yeah.

372
00:20:45,320 --> 00:20:46,180
Bucket relay!

373
00:20:46,180 --> 00:20:46,640
Here.

374
00:20:48,100 --> 00:20:48,500
Next!

375
00:20:48,500 --> 00:20:59,140
Whaaaaat?

376
00:20:59,140 --> 00:21:00,320
Whaaaaat?

377
00:21:12,540 --> 00:21:14,600
Let's leave the rest to the pros.

378
00:21:15,140 --> 00:21:15,580
Right.

379
00:21:15,580 --> 00:21:20,080
That firefighter drenched us
like we were his sworn enemies.

380
00:21:20,740 --> 00:21:22,980
That's what firefighters do.

381
00:21:22,980 --> 00:21:25,020
Thanks for your hard work.

382
00:21:27,700 --> 00:21:30,320
Still, soaked like this, we'll catch a cold.

383
00:21:34,440 --> 00:21:36,880
I think I just heard a fire engine's siren.

384
00:21:37,260 --> 00:21:37,600
Yeah.

385
00:21:38,940 --> 00:21:41,860
Fine. You go sleep by yourself.

386
00:21:56,020 --> 00:21:56,500
Hup!

387
00:21:56,980 --> 00:21:57,960
Thanks for waiting!

388
00:21:57,960 --> 00:21:59,040
Thanks, pal.

389
00:21:59,040 --> 00:22:00,420
Here you go.

390
00:22:00,420 --> 00:22:01,920
Ow ow!

391
00:22:03,240 --> 00:22:07,860
I'll take the ganmodoki and daikon.

392
00:22:08,720 --> 00:22:10,700
And I'll have the chikuwabu and tsumire.

393
00:22:11,180 --> 00:22:12,320
And konnyaku.

394
00:22:12,320 --> 00:22:13,020
Coming right up.

395
00:22:13,020 --> 00:22:14,420
Wait a second.

396
00:22:14,780 --> 00:22:15,680
I'm broke.

397
00:22:16,100 --> 00:22:17,180
Don't worry about it.

398
00:22:17,620 --> 00:22:19,760
I swiped some from Mom's wallet.

399
00:22:20,240 --> 00:22:21,500
Nice work, Dad.

400
00:22:21,500 --> 00:22:23,120
You haven't changed a
bit since the old days.

401
00:22:23,840 --> 00:22:26,000
Idiot, keep it from Mom.

402
00:22:26,540 --> 00:22:30,600
If she chases us around like she did during that Ryozuke Rebellion,
we'll be in real trouble.

403
00:22:31,540 --> 00:22:32,760
Anyway,

404
00:22:32,760 --> 00:22:33,740
Cheers!

405
00:22:35,440 --> 00:22:36,680
That really hits home.

406
00:22:36,680 --> 00:22:37,360
Honestly.

407
00:22:38,640 --> 00:22:39,980
Still, well,

408
00:22:41,700 --> 00:22:47,480
you were a hopeless case, so it's a blessing
you never ended up causing the police any trouble.

409
00:22:48,100 --> 00:22:50,900
Well, in a different sense,
you're still a burden.

410
00:22:50,900 --> 00:22:52,480
That's right, I almost forgot.

411
00:22:53,120 --> 00:22:55,200
I had something to give to the old man.

412
00:22:55,200 --> 00:22:56,140
Here you go.

413
00:22:57,420 --> 00:22:59,720
Kankichi, you... this is...

414
00:23:00,280 --> 00:23:02,800
I bought it earlier at Ameyoko.

415
00:23:03,420 --> 00:23:05,220
It's your birthday tomorrow, isn't it?

416
00:23:07,740 --> 00:23:11,080
You bought it with your salary,
so it's probably cheap junk anyway.

417
00:23:11,520 --> 00:23:13,980
It looks like the one from back then,
doesn't it?

418
00:23:13,980 --> 00:23:15,380
Well, yeah.

419
00:23:15,380 --> 00:23:16,360
Ryotsu

420
00:23:16,360 --> 00:23:17,980
Chief?

421
00:23:18,220 --> 00:23:20,560
May I join in too?

422
00:23:21,080 --> 00:23:22,660
Go right ahead, go ahead. Here, Kankichi.

423
00:23:23,120 --> 00:23:23,600
To the map...

424
00:23:25,800 --> 00:23:28,180
Looks like there was a fire right nearby

425
00:23:28,960 --> 00:23:32,560
They say the two who fought the fire so
bravely left without even giving their names.

426
00:23:34,100 --> 00:23:36,640
They must have been a close father and son.

427
00:23:37,440 --> 00:23:39,920
I hear they left in perfect sync.

428
00:23:42,760 --> 00:23:44,300
Let's drink the night away.

429
00:23:44,720 --> 00:23:46,020
I'm in a good mood, somehow.

430
00:23:46,800 --> 00:23:47,360
Nice.

431
00:23:48,140 --> 00:23:50,520
Old man, keep the sake coming!

432
00:23:50,520 --> 00:23:51,020
Coming right up.

433
00:23:52,620 --> 00:23:54,580
What a drinking pace you have, Chief.

434
00:23:54,580 --> 00:23:58,260
Chief, the konjac here is good,
and the ganmo is delicious too.

435
00:23:58,260 --> 00:24:01,020
Then I'll have some of that too.

436
00:24:01,020 --> 00:24:02,060
And the hanpen too.

437
00:24:14,840 --> 00:24:17,100
Summer has come again this year.

438
00:24:17,100 --> 00:24:19,720
It's here, it's here,
it's here, it's here, it's here!

439
00:24:19,720 --> 00:24:22,980
Summer has come again this year.

440
00:24:22,980 --> 00:24:25,040
It's here, it's here, it's here!

441
00:24:25,040 --> 00:24:28,620
Drink it all on the big road, yajukui no

442
00:24:28,620 --> 00:24:34,440
Drink it all on the big road, yajukui no

443
00:24:34,440 --> 00:24:35,820
Agisame

444
00:24:38,360 --> 00:24:40,820
Summer has come again this year.

445
00:24:40,820 --> 00:24:43,540
It's here, it's here, it's here, it's here!

446
00:24:43,540 --> 00:24:46,740
Summer has come again this year.

447
00:24:47,100 --> 00:24:49,280
Boketa, boketa, zeketa, bokkashina

448
00:24:49,280 --> 00:24:51,320
Big wave, little wave, chikkui

449
00:24:51,320 --> 00:24:52,240
about the size of that one

450
00:24:52,240 --> 00:24:55,100
minami kaze ni hoi

451
00:24:55,100 --> 00:24:57,240
Big Yoshiri, little Yoshiri, chikkui

452
00:24:57,240 --> 00:24:58,400
about the size of that one

453
00:24:58,400 --> 00:24:59,520
Akusare

454
00:24:59,520 --> 00:25:01,160
Bori bori bori bori bori

455
00:25:01,160 --> 00:25:02,020
Bori bori bori bori bori

456
00:25:02,780 --> 00:25:04,280
Aaaaaah!

457
00:25:05,400 --> 00:25:08,360
Minami kaze ni hoi

458
00:25:08,360 --> 00:25:10,580
Aaaaaaa

459
00:25:11,360 --> 00:25:14,300
Minami kaze ni hoi

460
00:25:14,300 --> 00:25:17,340
Ah ah ah ah ah

461
00:25:17,340 --> 00:25:20,520
On the shore, umpuru, on the shore, umpuri

462
00:25:20,520 --> 00:25:22,140
Poro poro poro poro poro poro poro

463
00:25:22,560 --> 00:25:23,320
Acchu

464
00:25:29,660 --> 00:25:32,520
How awful! What a terrible script this is!

465
00:25:32,800 --> 00:25:34,920
With that play at the
retirement home just now,

466
00:25:34,920 --> 00:25:38,900
why do we have to be in
an all-girls swim meet?

467
00:25:39,360 --> 00:25:43,340
Honestly, letting Ryotsu
write the script was a mistake.

468
00:25:44,300 --> 00:25:47,440
Next time, the classic Momotelera.
See you then.

